Description: VeltOS Office: LibreOffice with Microsoft 365's start screen
 The word processor, spreadsheet and presentation programs of LibreOffice
 (Debian) set up for people who come from Microsoft Office: each starts on
 a Windows 11 start screen like Microsoft 365's (Home with a greeting,
 blank document and templates, recent and pinned files with search; New;
 Open; Account; Options) in the app's colour, with the entrance
 animations of Windows 11. VeltOS' own templates (meeting notes, report,
 to-do list, monthly budget, invoice, expense tracker, weekly schedule)
 come with LibreOffice's.
 .
 The window frame gives LibreOffice's windows the app's colour in the
 title bar (Word blue, Excel green, PowerPoint orange).
 The configuration layer gives LibreOffice the ribbon-like "Tabbed"
 interface, the Colibre icons, .docx/.xlsx/.pptx as the default file
 formats without a question on every save, fonts with the metrics of the
 common Windows fonts, the name "VeltOS Office" in window titles, and no
 donation or release-notes bars. Users' own settings in LibreOffice take
 precedence. It is LibreOffice underneath.
